#
# D-150 — WHICH REQUIREMENT FAMILIES EXIST WAS A HAND-TYPED LITERAL, SIX TIMES.
#
#     \b(?:US|FR|NFR|AC|VC|IR|TR)-\d+(?:\.\d+)?\b
#
# appeared in four modules, and every copy knew the same seven families. This
# spec carries 71 requirement IDs and 15 of them are GI- and OT-, so an
# observable truth was invisible to every one of those readers at once: never
# counted by the DONE gate, never given a synthesized verdict row, never seen as
# covered by a casting that cites it — and, because the evidence binder reads
# the same literal, never bindable to an evidence file at all. EVID-02 could not
# bind evidence to an observable truth because nothing in the pipeline agreed
# that observable truths were requirements.
#
# THE SHAPE OF THE FIX IS THE POINT. Six copies of one rule is the escalated
# class stated plainly: the axis (which families) was hand-bound at every site
# that consumed it. The families are now ONE declaration in `schemas.vocab`,
# and the pattern is BUILT from that prefix set rather than typed beside it, so
# adding a family is one edit and every reader sees it the same day. Casting 3
# owns the export (LOCKED name `REQUIREMENT_ID_RE`) and the package-wide scan
# that reports any module still carrying its own copy; the four sites in this
# casting's files — `foundry_validate.py` x3 and `foundry_orchestrator.py`'s
# `_REQ_ID_RE` — read it.
#
# NFR-002 IS THE FIRST ASSERTION, NOT AN AFTERTHOUGHT. The declared pattern is
# a strict SUPERSET of the literal it replaces, so every ID that was counted
# before is still counted; the table proves that family by family rather than
# claiming it. A widening that quietly dropped VC-, IR- or TR- would be a
# narrowing wearing the word.
#
# THE ADJACENT PATH: the requirement COUNT is the reader the defect names; P3
# VERDICT SYNTHESIS is a different caller of the same id source, and it writes
# one row per id while `verdict_coverage` is measured against the count. If the
# two ever read different families the run reports coverage over a denominator
# that does not match its own rows. The table drives both and asserts they
# agree.
